{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/41346-v20-w20-additional-books-question","id":41346,"title":"V20 & W20 additional books question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-02T14:57:19-08:00","id":41346,"title":"V20 & W20 additional books question","content":"What background/fluff books should I get for to expand my knowledge of each world (and I guess M20 if that information is available)?<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> <br /> Aric<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1886-wolfx","name":"Wolfx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T15:22:14-08:00","id":41356,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of material out there so it really depends on what you're looking for exactly. Just looking for stuff on the various Factions and groups within each race? Their history? Politics? Realms beyond Earth? I mean I could throw together a list for each line but it would be pretty board and general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T03:47:26-08:00","id":41611,"title":"","content":"I would like more information on the factions and groups within each race, and histories. I am slowly trying to get back into the classic line and it is all very overwhelming. <br /> <br /> Thanks for your help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1886-wolfx","name":"Wolfx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T09:24:36-08:00","id":41768,"title":"","content":"Well to be fair V20 and W20 do a nice job of summarizing what you're looking for but if you're looking for more here goes.<br /> <br /> Vampire: the Masquerade:<br /> <br /> V20 Companion*<br /> The Rev Ed Clan Books<br /> Guide to the Camarilla<br /> Guide to the Anarchs<br /> Guide to the Sabbat<br /> <br /> These books nicely cover what you're looking for in terms of the groups and factions within Kindred society. With the Clan Books, if you can't afford all of them, I'd focus first on those of Clans you're most interested in** and the Independent Clans. There are books that handle special groups within the Sects, like the Black Hand and Templars and they are pretty good but aren't all that necessary. Oh and take Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand with a grain of salt, it's a crazy, controversial and it's creator may have intended it as a middle finger to the company as he was leaving.<br /> <br /> *I know V20 Companion tends to get a lot of hate but it isn't actually all that bad. Could more have been put into? Of course but then I could point dozens upon dozens that could as well.<br /> <br /> **The same with the Tribe and Tradition Books.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages: Vampire (as well as the entire Dark Ages line) is definitely worth a look as well.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: the Apocalypse:<br /> <br /> W20 Rage Across the World<br /> Rev Ed Tribe Books<br /> Book of Auspices<br /> Past Lives<br /> Player's Guide to the Garou<br /> <br /> Mage: the Ascension:<br /> <br /> Guide to the Traditions<br /> Guide to the Technocracy*<br /> Rev Ed Tradition and Convention Books**<br /> <br /> Also worth picking is Initiates of the Art, Bitter Road and Masters of the Art as they present a nice spread spread on the three levels of mages out there, Initiate, Disciple and Master.<br /> <br /> *This book is nearly a full Rulebook in its own right and has everything you need to create characters of the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> **It's worth noting that the Convention Books for the NWO, Syndicate, Progenitors and VE were recently created as they were never done before the line ended. I also highly recommend them as all four are truly excellent books even if you aren't a Technocrat fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}